// schedule-v1: cap=64 events=512; in0=i64:3; in0=i64:-1; in1=i64:7; in0=i64:4; in0=i64:-1; in0=i64:2; in1=i64:1

// x-engine-collections-02: collection slots paused by a bottom source wake without
// the fire catch-up a woken select arm gets: the in1 fire during the bottom window
// (epoch 3) is lost.
// command: graphix-fuzz run design/review-2026-10-12/repro/x-engine-collections-02.gx
// expected, as the select-arm twin `select in0 { n if n >= 0 => [in1 ~ n], _ => never() }`
// gives: Trace([0:[0]]; [0:[0]]; []; []; [0:[4]]; []; [0:[4]]; [0:[2]])
// observed, interp and jit alike, every session mode:
//   Trace([0:[0]]; []; []; []; [0:[0]]; []; [0:[0]]; [0:[2]])
// With `|x| count(in1) + x` as the callback and the schedule cut after in0=4, the map
// stays bottom at the return (trace ends []), where the select twin gives [5].
// The same loss under array::fold.
let xs = select in0 { n if n >= 0 => [n], _ => never() };
array::map(xs, |x| in1 ~ x)
